; THE CROSSWAY POST (Phase 38M2) — the wardens' gate on the road north, and the place 38M's toll is
; actually about. 38M built the toll, the permit and the bribe and left them standing in the town
; square because there was nowhere else to put them; this is that somewhere.
;
; ⚠️ ORIENTATION. World z DECREASES going north, so the player arrives from the SOUTH — local z = +26
; is the seam with wilds_north, and the road runs north (−z) through the gate at z = 0 and out the far
; side to the portal beyond. Everything in this file is LOCAL to the cell's own origin; the streamer
; places the cell at Center (0, 0, -116). Reading a transform out of here and using it as a world
; point is the 37C bug and lands 116 m south of where it was authored.
;
; ⚠️ THE GATE IS A GAP, NOT AN ARCH. prp_gate_palisade is a closed palisade with two towers — there is
; no opening in the model. The road passes BETWEEN two of them: each is 15.93 m wide and centred at
; x = ±11.9, so their inner edges land at x = ±3.94 and the 8 m road runs clean through the 7.88 m
; gap. That arithmetic is here rather than eyeballed, because the .tscn shows nothing about it and a
; palisade half a metre too far in is a wall across the only route in the cell.
;
; ⚠️ EVERYTHING STATIC PARENTS TO Nav. Geometry outside the NavigationRegion3D is not carved into the
; navmesh, so an NPC walks straight through a palisade that looks solid. The two wardens deliberately
; do NOT — only static geometry should carve.
;
; ⚠️ NO RAISED GROUND ANYWHERE (38K's engine finding). CharacterBody3D has no step-up, so a kerb is an
; invisible wall the navmesh happily paths NPCs over. The road is a 6 cm skin with NO COLLIDER; the
; height in this cell comes from an 8 m tower and a 5.5 m palisade, from props and never from terrain.
;
; LAYOUT, south (the approach from the wilds) to north (through the gate):
;   z +26..+12  the approach: dead pines and rock closing both verges down to the road, one brazier.
;   z +12..+2   the queue: the waystone, the caravan yard east of the road (carts, crates, hay, a
;               fence line and a cook-fire) and the wardens' compound west of it, with the well and
;               two benches for the people waiting. This is where the warden and the gate-hand stand.
;   z  0        the gate line: two palisades and two watch towers, banner on the west tower.
;   z -6        the far side, and the region portal (authored on RegionResource.PortalPoint, not
;               here) — so a player pays or produces papers BEFORE the crossing, never after.

[sub_resource type="NavigationMesh" id="NavMesh_crossway"]
geometry_parsed_geometry_type = 1
cell_size = 0.25
cell_height = 0.25
agent_height = 1.75
agent_radius = 0.5
agent_max_climb = 0.5

[sub_resource type="BoxMesh" id="BoxMesh_floor"]
size = Vector3(52, 0.5, 52)

[sub_resource type="BoxShape3D" id="Shape_floor"]
size = Vector3(52, 0.5, 52)

; Colder and greyer than either the square's packed earth or the market's swept flagstones — this is
; the last of the valley before the Reach, and the ground is meant to read as leaving somewhere.
[sub_resource type="StandardMaterial3D" id="Mat_floor"]
albedo_color = Color(0.27, 0.27, 0.25, 1)
roughness = 0.95

; The road itself: the one lighter surface in the cell, so the route through is legible from the seam.
[sub_resource type="StandardMaterial3D" id="Mat_road"]
albedo_color = Color(0.42, 0.38, 0.32, 1)
roughness = 0.9

; The yard's hardstanding, east of the road, so the caravan ground reads as a different room.
[sub_resource type="StandardMaterial3D" id="Mat_yard"]
albedo_color = Color(0.33, 0.31, 0.28, 1)
roughness = 0.88

; The ONE warm accent (ART_STYLE §7): coals in the braziers and under the cook-fire, the OmniLights
; and nothing else in the cell glows.
[sub_resource type="StandardMaterial3D" id="Mat_ember"]
albedo_color = Color(0.62, 0.22, 0.08, 1)
emission_enabled = true
emission = Color(1, 0.45, 0.12, 1)
emission_energy_multiplier = 3.0

[sub_resource type="SphereMesh" id="Mesh_coals"]
radius = 0.13
height = 0.26
radial_segments = 8
rings = 4

; --- Ground skins. NO COLLIDERS on any of them (see the step-up note above). Sized to ABUT, never to
; --- overlap: two coplanar slabs z-fight along their seam and that is invisible from the .tscn.
; ---   road   x -4 .. +4,  the full 52 m of the cell
; ---   yard   x +5 .. +19, z -2 .. +12
; 38Q2, the caravan board. Built from primitives rather than a model, and that is the second answer
; to this question: prp_banner_guild was placed here first (it is what the Embermarket's notice board
; uses) and rejected on the render for two reasons at once. It is a hanging cloth PENNANT, so at
; reading distance it fills the view as a red sheet with no surface to post anything on — and this
; cell already spends that model on GateBanner, "the only thing in the cell that says whose road this
; is". Two identical pennants forty feet apart would have diluted the one that means something.
