; --- The hired sword (Phase 38R) -------------------------------------------------
; Wren Halloway, a caravan guard between contracts. Five hundred gold puts her in the party through
; service.crossway.mercenary, and the whole hire happens in CONVERSATION — she carries a
; DialogueComponent and no ServiceComponent, because DialogueEffect.OpenService now exists and a
; person you hire by pressing E on her is a vending machine with a face.
;
; ⚠️ THIS CELL HAD FOUR SERVICES AND NOT ONE CONVERSATION until now, which 38Q2 recorded as a finding
; when it went looking for somewhere to mention the board. The four wardens are all counters on
; purpose — a permit, a bribe, a search and a fine are transactions, not talk. A sword for hire is
; the opposite, and is the cell's first speaking part.
;
; ⚠️ CompanionRecruiterComponent is what keeps her from standing here while she also walks behind the
; player (32E). It hides the body AND its collider, so the interaction prompt goes with it, and it
; re-derives from GameLoadedEvent rather than trusting the recruit event a streamed-in cell missed.
; Without it a hired Wren is in two places, and the second one can be hired again.
;
; ⚠️ The body is npc_adventurer_f — the same model Sera wears in the Embermarket. 38Q2's duplicate
; rule is about two identical models IN ONE FRAME; these two are cells apart. What IS in frame here
; are the two guild-body wardens four metres up the road, which is why she wears a fighter's kit and
; not the guild coat: she works this road, she does not police it.
;
; She is NOT parented to Nav: only static geometry should carve the navmesh.
; ⚠️ POSITION AND YAW ARE THE RENDERED ANSWERS. The first placement, (10.6, 0, 6.4), was three metres
; due south of the caravan board — which is exactly where a player stands to READ the board, so she
; blocked the one interactable this cell shipped last sub-phase. Nothing in the .tscn said so; the
; front-on shot came back with the board filling the frame behind her. 38Q's "render the people AND
; the furniture together" fired again, on a prop that was not even hers.
; ⚠️ And the body faces +Z, not Godot's -Z: the identity transform pointed her at the board's back.
; The yaw below is the same basis CartA carries, and turns her west across the yard to the road.
[node name="Mercenary" type="Node3D" parent="."]
transform = Transform3D(0, 0, -1, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, 0, 12.6, 0, 8.9)
script = ExtResource("2_entity")
DisplayName = "Wren Halloway"
TemplateId = "npc.mercenary"

